exercises.instructions:
Write three functions:

**createEvent(title, month, day)** — returns an event object. If day < 1 or day > 31, return the string `"Error: [day] is not a valid day"`.
```js
createEvent('Dinner', 'July', 15)
// { title: 'Dinner', month: 'July', day: 15 }
createEvent('Party', 'June', 35)
// "Error: 35 is not a valid day"
```

**createCalendar(owner, events)** — returns a calendar object with owner and events array.
```js
createCalendar('Amy', [event1, event2])
// { owner: 'Amy', events: [event1, event2] }
```

**reportMonthlyEvents(calendar, month)** — returns only the events matching the given month.
```js
reportMonthlyEvents(cal, 'July')
// [{ title: 'Dinner', month: 'July', day: 15 }, ...]
```

